## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates designing scalable, secure, cross-account data access across tenants with strong isolation and auditable sharing.

## Key Concepts
- Lake Formation catalog-based permissions
- S3 per-tenant prefixes and object ownership
- KMS key policies for residency and encryption
- IAM SCPs and cross-account sharing, data marts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tenant user policy (pseudo)
{
  'Version': '2012-10-17',
  'Statement': [
    {'Effect': 'Allow', 'Action': ['lakeformation:GrantPermissions', 's3:GetObject'], 'Resource': ['arn:aws:s3:::corp-data/tenant-id-*/**']}
  ]
}

// Data-mart role policy (pseudo)
{
  'Version': '2012-10-17',
  'Statement': [
    {'Effect': 'Allow', 'Action': ['lakeformation:SelectFromDataCatalog'], 'Resource': '*'}
  ]
}

// Cross-account share policy (pseudo)
{
  'Version': '2012-10-17',
  'Statement': [
    {'Effect': 'Allow', 'Action': ['glue:GetTable','s3:GetObject'], 'Resource': ['arn:aws:glue:*:*:catalog','arn:aws:s3:::shared-data/**']}
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor and alert on policy drift?
- What are the trade-offs of using Lake Formation versus direct IAM policies for data access?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design scalable, auditable data-lake isolation using Lake Formation, IAM tagging, and cross-account roles; also assesses policy drafting and test planning.

## Key Concepts

- Lake Formation permissions and data location mapping
- IAM tags and condition keys
- Cross-account roles and trust policies
- S3 tenant prefixes and data encryption with KMS
- Admin audit paths and automated tests

## Code Example

```json
{
  "PolicySnippet": {
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
        "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-id/*",
        "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "LFPolicySnippet": {
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantRole"},
    "Permissions": ["SELECT","DESCRIBE","ALTER"],
    "DataLocation": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-id/"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy changes without impacting production data?
- What are the trade-offs of Lake Formation vs direct IAM/S3 controls in this scenario?

